G2443.def:
ἵνα, 
__I. adverb (poët., Hom., al.), 
__1. of place, where, whither. 
__2. of circumstance, when. 
__II. Conjunction, 
__1. prop., final, denoting purpose or end (cl.), that, in order that, usually the first word in the clause, but sometimes (cl. also) preceded by an emphatic word (Actes 19:4, Romains 11:31 (?), Galates 2:10, al.); 
__(a) with optative (so in cl. after historic tenses): after a pres., Éphésiens 1:17 (but WH, mg., subjc.; see Burton, §225, Rem., 2); 
__(b) with subjc.: after a pres., Marc 4:21, Luc 6:34, Jean 3:15, Actes 2:25, Romains 1:11, al.; after a pf., Matthieu 1:22, Jean 5:23 1 Corinthiens 9:22, al.; after an imperat. (present or aor.), Matthieu 7:1, Marc 11:25, Jean 10:38, 1 Corinthiens 7:5, al.; after a delib. subjc., Marc 1:38, al.; after a fut., Luc 16:4, Jean 14:3, 1 Corinthiens 15:28, al.; after historic tenses (where optative in cl.; WM, 359f.; M, Pr., 196f.), Marc 6:41 (impf.), Jean 4:8 (plpf.), Marc 3:14 (aor.), al.; 
__(with) in late writers (M, Pr., 35; Burton, §§198, 199), with indic., fut: Luc 20:10, 1 Pierre 3:1, al.; 
__(d) as often in eccl. writers (Thayer, see word), with indic. pres.: 1 Corinthiens 4:6, Galates 4:17, al. (?; but V. Burton, §198, Rem.); 
__(e) εἰς (διὰ) τοῦτο, ἵνα: Jean 18:37, 1 Timothée 1:16, al.; τούτου χάριν, Tite 1:5; 
__(f) elliptical constructions: omission of the principal verb, Jean 1:8, 2 Thessaloniciens 3:9, 1 Jean 2:19, al.; of the final verb, Romains 4:16, 2 Corinthiens 8:13, al. 
__2. In late writers, definitive, = inf. (WM, 420; Bl, §69, 1), that; 
__(a) after verbs of wishing, caring, striving, etc.: θέλω, Matthieu 7:12, al.; ζητῶ, 1 Corinthiens 4:2 14:12; ζηλόω, 1 Corinthiens 14:1, al.; 
__(b) after verbs of saying, asking, exhorting: εἰπεῖν, Matthieu 4:3, al.; ἐρωτῶ, Marc 7:26, al.; παρακαλῶ, Matthieu 14:36, 1 Corinthiens 1:10, al., etc.; 
__(with) after words expressing expediency, etc.: συμφέρει, Matthieu 18:6, Jean 11:50, al.; ἱκανός, Matthieu 8:8, Luc 7:6; χρείαν ἔχω, Jean 2:25, al, etc.; 
__(d) after substantives, adding further definition: ὥρα, Jean 12:23 13:1; χρόνος, Apocalypse 2:21; συνήθεια, Jean 18:39; μισθός, 1 Corinthiens 9:18. 
__3. In late writers, ecbatic, denoting the result, = ὥστε, that, so that (M, Pr., 206ff.; WM, 572; Bl., §69, 3; Burton, §223): Romains 11:11, 1 Corinthiens 7:29, 1 Thessaloniciens 5:4, al. (but see Thayer, see word); so with the formula referring to the fulfilment of prophecy, ἵνα πληρωθῇ, Matthieu 1:22 2:14, Jean 13:18, al.

G2452.def:
Ἰουδαϊκῶς 
adv.; 
in Jewish fashion: Galates 2:14.†

G2478.def:
ἰσχυρός, -ά, -όν
(ἰσχύω), [in LXX for אֵל, גִּבּוֹר, עָצוּם, חָזַק, etc. ;] 
strong, mighty, powerful; 
__(a) of persons, as to body or spirit: Matthieu 12:29, Marc 3:27, Luc 11:21-22, 1 Corinthiens 4:10 (opposite to ἀσθενής), Hébreux 11:34 (ἐν πολέμῳ), Apocalypse 5:2 10:1 18:21 19:18; οἱ πλούσιοι κ. οἱ ἰ, Apocalypse 6:15; τὰ ἰ. = oἱ ἰ. (cf. 4Ki.24:15), 1 Corinthiens 1:27; of God (cf. Deutéronome 10:17), Apocalypse 18:8; compar., Matthieu 3:11, Marc 1:7, Luc 11:22, 1 Corinthiens 1:25 (τὸ ἀσθενὲς τ. θεοῦ) 1 Corinthiens 10:22; 
__(b) of things: λιμός, Luc 15:14; ἐπιστολαί ( βαρεῖαι κ. ἰ.), 2 Corinthiens 10:10; κραυγή, Hébreux 5:7; φωνή, Apocalypse 18:2; παράκλησις, Hébreux 6:18; πόλις, Apocalypse 18:10; βρονταί, Apocalypse 19:6.†
